<title>UK: Salomon sets call warrants on four U.S stocks.</title>
<headline>Salomon sets call warrants on four U.S stocks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salomon Brothers AG said it has issued one million American-style call warrants each on shares of Boeing Company, General Electric Company, IBM Corporation and Philip Morris Companies Inc. Five warrants control one share.</p>
<p>* * * *</p>
<p> EXERCISE PERIOD 11.AUG.97-18.DEC.98   PAYDATE	11.AUG.97</p>
<p> LISTING	   FFT/DUES</p>
<p> NOTES	     PRICES QUOTED ON REUTER PAGE  FFSS</p>
<p>* * * *</p>
<p> WARRANT	   STRIKE    ISSUE	PREMIUM</p>
<p> BOEING	    $58	 4.60 DEM   21.31 PCT</p>
<p> GEC		 $70	 4.46 DEM   17.24 PCT</p>
<p> IBM		$100	 7.82 DEM   21.14 PCT</p>
<p> PHILIP MORRIS   $45	 3.28 DEM   19.74 PCT</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
